foundation.css adopts app/globals.css tokens and Tailwind theme mappings.
Controls.tsx adapts components/atoms/Button.tsx, Switch.tsx,
SegmentedControl.tsx and the table grammar of primitives/RecordsTable.tsx.
Compositions.tsx and application.css derive navigation from SidebarNav.tsx,
resource lists from RecordsTable.tsx / TaskRows.tsx, statuses from
StatusPill.tsx, and information surfaces from ContextCards.tsx.
Conversation.tsx adapts ChatComposer.tsx, PromptBar.tsx, ToolChips.tsx,
TaskRows.tsx, ApprovalCard.tsx and AgentScreen.tsx visual structure.

Adaptations use only caller-supplied state, content, authority and callbacks.
No gallery demo records, timers, remote artwork, scripted assistant output,
commercial icons, analytics or website dependencies are included.
Existing platform-owned SVG paths are retained in Glyph.tsx.
Base UI supplies accessible unstyled interaction behavior, not visual tokens.

Application extensions: native field/input/textarea contracts, semantic
compound slots, accessible brand-derived accent and foreground, local
spacing scale (4px base), typography scale (12/13/14/16/20/24px), modal
geometry, live reduced-motion policy, responsive navigation, and required
computer layouts. These additions are not claimed as upstream APIs.

Inter Variable and JetBrains Mono Variable are bundled locally from
@fontsource-variable packages; no runtime Google Fonts request is made.
Their full SIL Open Font License notices are distributed in
public/licenses/inter-OFL.txt and public/licenses/jetbrains-mono-OFL.txt.

Bundled dependency notices are distributed in
public/licenses/beautiful-ui-dependencies.txt. That plain-text file retains
the installed Base UI (react/utils), Floating UI (react-dom/dom/core/utils),
clsx, tailwind-merge, use-sync-external-store, reselect, shadow-plugin and
Tailwind CSS MIT notices, plus class-variance-authority's full Apache 2.0
license. It also retains the Adobe Apache 2.0 and original Facebook MIT
attribution for virtual-event routines vendored by Base UI / Floating UI.
These dependency licenses are separate from Beautiful UI's MIT license.
The existing static publisher includes public assets without a separate
license-generation step.
